  "bounded_policy_verification": {
    "source": "Figures 5.2, 5.4–5.6, 5.9–5.16, E.1–E.4. Normalize NORMAL_REM to NORMAL_REMOVE and supply the missing op in the printed two-argument call to the three-argument noOtherElementsAffected (the appendix supplies all three). The executable reconstruction retains E.3’s disjunction of implications. The separately checked only_one_kind_in_history obligation states its operational one-kind consequence.",
    "scope": "Unmodified stamped FIFO reconstruction with the three numbered policies per operation kind, no overrides. For any color and any replica, admit every time-oriented transitive causal relation on at most replicas × operations stamps, and any causally closed local history prefix and next operation. Prove pointwise properties independently of other colors. When all replicas finish, all know precisely the same operation records, establishing convergence and equal total queries. A sat query needs a concrete witness for the protocol: the disabled rule has one.",
